    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53083": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty - Chemical & Biological Engineering",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001459P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Engineering Primary Unit Chemical & Biological Engineering Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 3010 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Department of Chemical Engineering invites applications for a Clinical Assistant Professor position. The successful candidate will be primarily responsible for delivering high-quality instruction, mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and supporting departmental educational initiatives. Key responsibilities include teaching core courses in chemical engineering such as:: • Unit Operations Laboratory • Engineering Capstone Design • Transport Phenomena • Fluid Mechanics • Chemical Reaction Engineering/Kinetics • Material and Energy Balance The faculty member will employ effective, student-centered teaching practices, maintain instructional excellence, assess student learning outcomes, and contribute to continuous curriculum improvement. The position also includes advising and mentoring student teams involved in senior design projects and experiential learning activities. In addition to teaching responsibilities, the Clinical Assistant Professor will serve as the faculty advisor for the American Institute of Chemical Engineers (AIChE) student chapter, supporting student professional development, leadership activities, industry engagement, and participation in regional and national AIChE events. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to departmental service activities, collaborate with faculty and industry stakeholders, maintain strong connections with the chemical engineering profession, and foster an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Unit/Department Summary Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering | University of Idaho Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 90% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 0% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications B.S. in Chemical Engineering and Ph.D. in a related field Minimum of one semester of teaching experience Hold or obtain a Professional Engineer (PE) license in the state of Idaho within 5 years of employment Preferred Qualifications Have excellent communication skills, both oral and written Industry experience Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a collaborative, interdisciplinary environment Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/11/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants First priority will be given to complete applications received by December 15, 2026. Applicants are asked to submit a CV, letter of application, statement of teaching, and contact information for 3 references. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho is supported in limited circumstances from existing visa holders. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
