    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53077": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty - Ecological Immunology",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Regular Faculty - Ecological Immunology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regular Faculty - Ecological Immunology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001457P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Regular Faculty - Ecological Immunology Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience and qualifications Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Science Primary Unit Biological Sciences Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Regular Faculty Position Control Number 4632 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.00 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Department of Biological Sciences at the University of Idaho invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Eco-Immunology. We seek an innovative scientist who investigates immune function in wild or free-ranging animals and uses these systems to address fundamental questions at the interface of immunology, ecology, evolution, and infectious disease. We are broadly interested in candidates whose research examines how immune responses vary among individuals, populations, species, or environments, and how this variation influences infection, disease, fitness, host–pathogen interactions, or population and community processes. Research approaches may span scales from molecular and cellular mechanisms to whole-organism, population, and evolutionary processes. We particularly welcome candidates who combine field studies of natural populations with experimental, molecular, genomic, serological, cellular, or computational approaches. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: · ecological and evolutionary immunology · immune function in wild animal populations · environmental influences on immunity and disease susceptibility · comparative and evolutionary immunology · immunological variation within and among natural populations · wildlife disease ecology and emerging infectious disease The successful candidate will establish an externally funded, internationally recognized research program; mentor undergraduate and graduate students; contribute to the intellectual life of the Department of Biological Sciences; and participate in interdisciplinary collaborations across the University of Idaho. The position offers opportunities to interact with faculty working in ecology and evolution, infectious disease, immunology, genomics, computational biology, mathematical biology, and host–pathogen interactions. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education in Biological Sciences. Depending on expertise and departmental needs, teaching may include courses in areas such as immunology, organismal biology, ecology, infectious disease, or related subjects, as well as development of advanced courses in the candidate’s area of specialization. The successful candidate will also mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Duties include teaching an average of 1.5 classes per academic year; maintaining an active research program that includes securing external funding to support research activities in area of expertise; mentoring undergraduate and graduate students; attending faculty meetings and departmental seminars; serving on department, college, and/or university committees. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/science/academics/biological-sciences Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 35% Scholarship & Creative Activity 55% Outreach & Extension 5% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in a field relevant to Ecological Immunology. A minimum of 2 years of post-doctoral research experience relevant to the proposed research program. An active research program or research expertise in the field of ecological immunology. Peer-reviewed publications in scientific journals. Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated potential to secure external research funding (e.g., grants, fellowships). Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate student researchers. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/11/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Open until filled, first review priority given to those who apply by January 3, 2027. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho is supported in limited circumstances from existing visa holders. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application Statement of Research Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
