    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52386": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty - Computer Science",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001439P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with Experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Engineering Primary Unit Computer Science Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 2925 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/17/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The University of Idaho College of Engineering seeks applicants for an Assistant Clinical Faculty member on an academic year appointment in the Department of Computer Science and Cybersecurity. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in computer science and cybersecurity, combining lectures with laboratory, project-based, and experiential learning. Instruction may be delivered locally, online, hybrid, across campuses, and through hands-on laboratory experiences. Candidates with practical industry experience, professional certifications, or applied research interests in cybersecurity are strongly encouraged to apply. Applicants should possess excellent written and oral communication skills and demonstrate a commitment to student success, mentorship, and continuous program improvement. Faculty are expected to contribute to departmental, college, and university service activities and to support the University’s mission of engaged learning and community impact. Unit/Department Summary Department of Computer Science and Cybersecurity | University of Idaho Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 90% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 0% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications An earned M.S. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a closely related field. Experience in written and oral communication. Experience working collaboratively. Experience teaching courses in Computer Science and Cybersecurity or related experience. Preferred Qualifications An earned Ph.D. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a closely related field. Demonstrated excellence in university-level instruction. Demonstrated experience supporting student growth and academic development and achievement. Demonstrated ability to successfully mentor and advise undergraduate students. Demonstrated interest and potential in pursuing and/or supporting research and scholarship activities. Interest in pursuing and supporting research and scholarship activities Demonstrated potential for learning and implementing innovative hands-on instructional methods. Demonstrated potential for delivering instruction in a variety of formats including, but not limited to, local, online, hybrid, hands-on, and laboratory. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 08/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants First consideration will be given to complete applications received by September 6, 2026. Complete application consists of: CV, Letter of Qualification, Statement of Teaching, Transcripts, List of 3 References. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Transcripts Letter of Qualification Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
