    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52353": {
      "title": "Extension Faculty, Canyon County- 4-H Youth Development - Southern District",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Extension Faculty, Canyon County- 4-H Youth Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Extension Faculty, Canyon County- 4-H Youth Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001438P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Extension Faculty, Canyon County- 4-H Youth Development Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with Experience Location Off Campus Location - Canyon County Extension/Caldwell Primary Division/College College of Agricultural & Life Sciences Primary Unit Southern District Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Extension Faculty Position Control Number 1343 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 10/12/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type County Extension Educator/Professorial Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The University of Idaho Southern District is seeking applications for a tenure-track Assistant Extension Educator. The Extension Educator provides leadership for the Canyon County 4-H Youth Development program while contributing to multi-county 4-H initiatives in a defined area of expertise. Responsibilities include leading county 4-H programming; recruiting, training, and supporting volunteers; and developing and delivering high-quality educational opportunities for youth. The Educator supervises a full-time 4-H Youth Development Program Coordinator and collaborates with five additional Extension educators who support youth programming throughout Canyon County. Working in partnership with University of Idaho faculty, community organizations, governmental agencies, volunteers, and clientele, the Educator plans, implements, evaluates, and communicates the impacts of research-based youth development programs at the county, multi-county, district, and state levels. The Educator also collaborates with district and statewide colleagues to strengthen educational initiatives, support volunteer and staff development, and advance a coordinated, high-quality 4-H program across Idaho. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/extension/county/canyon Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 0% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 90% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications A master’s degree from an accredited institution in Youth Development, Adult Learning, Agriculture and Extension Education, Social Work, Human Development, or a closely related field. The degree must be completed by the date of hire. Experience providing organizational structure, guidance, and support for youth, families, and/or volunteers Experience adapting research-based information for oral and written presentations Experience developing and delivering educational programs for youth, volunteers, and/or community partners Experience using technology to market programs, deliver educational content, and communicate with stakeholders Preferred Qualifications Experience in Extension Education and 4-H Youth Development (relevant experience acquired within the last 5 years preferred). Experience recruiting, teaching, organizing, and managing volunteers Experience in needs assessment and program evaluation Experience in disseminating research results through scholarly outlets such as refereed /peer reviewed publications and/or presentations to peer audiences Experience in supervising Experience with grantsmanship Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Ability to lift, carry and/or otherwise move 50 lbs. Possess a valid driver’s license Work a flexible schedule, including some evenings and weekends. Posting Information Posting Date 07/31/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by August 31, 2026,will receive first consideration. Along with your online application, write a letter of qualification addressing how you meet the required and preferred qualifications listed. https://share.google/U5NhHXpesNfOL1kEH In addition, your application materials must include a CV, names & contact information for at least three (3) professional references, and unofficial transcripts. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Transcripts Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow,